WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:04.539
A.I Triage System. Two-minute demo.

2
00:00:05.391 --> 00:00:12.447
A nurse who uses a screen reader signs in. New notes arrive. Claude finds the evidence; people decide.

3
00:00:13.293 --> 00:00:20.047
The official order: top is seen first. Colors show urgency. The AI can never move a patient.

4
00:00:20.885 --> 00:00:24.687
A new note for Patient B arrives…

5
00:00:26.301 --> 00:00:32.148
Screen reader hears: “New evidence awaiting clinical review.” No name, no symptom. Order unchanged.

6
00:00:32.158 --> 00:00:36.489
Exact quotes from the note, labeled AI-assisted and unverified.

7
00:00:37.439 --> 00:00:41.770
It caught the change: denied at triage, now reported.

8
00:00:42.626 --> 00:00:47.865
And kept the mother’s history separate. A keyword search gets this wrong.

9
00:00:47.878 --> 00:00:53.420
What Claude received: two short excerpts. No name, no record number, no dates.

10
00:00:53.437 --> 00:00:58.982
Riley checks it against the real note and accepts. Saved with her name.

11
00:00:58.996 --> 00:01:05.142
Riley goes back to Patient A. Meanwhile the charge nurse approves Level 1 for B…

12
00:01:06.507 --> 00:01:13.868
B jumps to the top, but Riley’s place stays on A. Enter opens Patient A, not the wrong patient.

13
00:01:13.891 --> 00:01:19.738
A rule flags a possible emergency for Patient D. Urgent alert, still no name.

14
00:01:19.752 --> 00:01:24.079
Any nurse checks it — and must write why.

15
00:01:24.091 --> 00:01:30.846
The charge nurse reads the reason and confirms. Patient D moves to Level 1, with full history.

16
00:01:30.856 --> 00:01:36.095
An Epic-style chart with tabs. Search the notes — matches light up.

17
00:01:36.103 --> 00:01:41.041
Hands busy? Speak: “bring up patient C.” Dictation writes notes too.

18
00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:47.251
If the AI goes down, notes still show up for manual review. Nothing is lost.

19
00:01:47.261 --> 00:01:52.505
The AI suggests. People decide. Accessible, private, and works without AI.

